    <!-- §3 Left Pane -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="left-pane">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§3</div>
        <h2>Left Pane — Corridor Selector</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Corridor Dropdown</h3>
      <p>Editable QComboBox with QCompleter (MatchContains, CaseInsensitive). Populated from <code>GET /api/v2/corridors</code>. Display format: <code>{flag} {SRC} → {flag} {DST}</code>. Fires on <code>activated</code> signal only — not on each keystroke.</p>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>
        <b>Endpoint shape &amp; scoping.</b> <code>GET /api/v2/corridors</code> returns
        <b>all active</b> corridors wrapped in a <code>data.corridors</code> envelope, and
        applies a jurisdiction filter <b>only</b> when <code>?source_country=</code> is
        passed (there is no per-scope gate on the list) — so any authenticated operator,
        including a compliance officer, can populate the selector. The client reads the
        nested <code>data.corridors</code> array, shows a
        <em>"— Select Active Bilateral Corridor —"</em> placeholder (with a warning log)
        when empty, and on corridor switch <b>auto-selects the highest-funded reserve pool</b>.
      </div></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-ok"><span class="dp-ci">✓</span><div>
        <b>Sandbox seeding — corridors &amp; reserve liquidity.</b> Default bilateral
        corridors (GHA-NGA, NGA-GHA, KEN-TZA, ZAF-ZWE) and reserve pools
        (<code>CBN-NGN-RESERVE-01</code> = 500M NGN, <code>BoG-GHS-RESERVE-01</code> = 500M
        GHS) are provisioned by <code>rake cvib:seed_corridors</code> and
        <code>rake cvib:seed_reserves</code> — both re-run automatically by
        <code>cvib:sandbox_reset</code>, so a reset never leaves Corridor Ops empty.
        A reserve pool's <b>available balance is DERIVED, not a stored column</b>: pool-01
        = <code>LiquidityLock.where(corridor, status:'active').sum(:amount)</code>, adjusted
        by <code>ReservePoolEvent</code> rebalances. To fund a pool you add an active
        <code>LiquidityLock</code> (the seed lock is claim-less) — never write a balance
        field.
      </div></div>

      <h4>On Change — Full Reload Cascade</h4>
      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load corridor identity</h4><p>GET /corridors/:id → ID, Code, Asset Code, Status, Agreement ID, Source, Target</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load FX rate</h4><p>GET /corridors/:id/fx_rate → sets current rate and FX snapshot labels</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load liquidity position</h4><p>GET /corridors/:id/liquidity_position → Domestic, Linked, Net labels</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load reserve pools</h4><p>GET /corridors/:id/reserve_pools → populates pool selector dropdown</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load active locks</h4><p>GET /api/v2/liquidity_locks?corridor_id=:id → populates active locks table</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>Load limits + apply status style</h4><p>GET /corridors/:id/limits → Risk Limits panel. applyCorridorStatusStyle() updates Danger Zone button.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3>Mode Selector</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Daily Cap</th><th>Per-Tx Cap</th><th>Velocity</th><th>Governance Required</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Pilot</strong></td><td>500,000 XOF</td><td>10,000 XOF</td><td>100,000/hr</td><td>All lock operations</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Supervised</strong></td><td>2,500,000 XOF</td><td>500,000 XOF</td><td>1,000,000/hr</td><td>Locks &gt; 1M, FX changes</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Production</strong></td><td>Per corridor config</td><td>Per corridor config</td><td>Per corridor config</td><td>FX changes, limit changes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
