      <h3>Pre-Demo Safeguards</h3>
      <p>Three conditions to verify before the walkthrough begins.</p>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div><strong>Position inertia (§5).</strong> With no corridor selected, the Liquidity Position pane is unpopulated and the left pane's Corridor Identity fields are blank. Selecting a corridor triggers a full reload that fills every read-only field. In the reference state, selecting <code>AGO → GMB</code> surfaces <strong>Net Position −1,500.00 GMD</strong> and <strong>Position Status ⚠ Deficit</strong> — the cold-start is honest about the shortfall, it does not zero it out.</div></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn"><span class="dp-ci">⚠</span><div><strong>Gateway health is live (§3).</strong> The corridor selector badge reflects real connectivity. The reference corridor reads <em>Gateway: Degraded — partial connectivity</em> with <strong>⚠ BREACH ALERT: WARNING</strong> in the header strip and <em>Corridor health: warning</em>. Brief the room that Execute Liquidity Action and <em>Settle via PAPSS</em> depend on gateway state — demonstrate the degraded path <em>before</em> claiming a clean settlement.</div></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-danger"><span class="dp-ci">⛔</span><div><strong>Danger Zone is one click from irreversible (§6).</strong> The right pane's Emergency actions (Manual recon, System override, Request support) and the red <strong>Deactivate Corridor</strong> control act on production ledger state. Keep Mode on the intended environment and do not exercise <em>Deactivate Corridor</em> or <em>System override</em> during a walkthrough — use Escalate to Governance to show the safe change path instead.</div></div>

